+# Worker Vulkan capture — M1 results
+
+**Branch:** `vulkan-capture-m1` (off `movietheater-fork`)
+**Date:** 2026-07-15, box Ziggy (RTX 4070 Ti)
+**Goal (spec §5):** LRPS2 `pcsx2_renderer: "paraLLEl-GS"` streams Stuntman in a live room through the
+existing CPU video path (readback), rendered via `RETRO_HW_CONTEXT_VULKAN`.
+
+**Headline:** the frontend half works end-to-end. paraLLEl-GS renders Stuntman at a flat 60 fps
+through the Vulkan→staging→CPU readback path, with correct colors, and survives room reuse. The one
+real finding is teardown: the core's `context_destroy` **deadlocks in our single-thread LibCo model**
+(the same MTGS::CloseGS wedge the GL path documents) — so, exactly like GL, ps2-Vulkan must ship with
+`skip_hw_context_destroy`. With that hack the close is clean and repeatable.
+
+---
+
+## What was implemented
+
+- **Vendored headers** (verbatim from the LRPS2 tree it tests against): `libretro_vulkan.h`,
+  `vulkan/{vk_platform.h,vulkan_core.h,vk_video/*}`, plus a minimal `vulkan/vulkan.h` (core only — we
+  never present). `vulkan-1.dll` is loaded at runtime; no SDK link (`VK_NO_PROTOTYPES`).
+- **`pkg/worker/caged/libretro/nanoarch/nanoarch_vulkan.c`** — the frontend half:
+  - negotiation v1 **and** v2 (paraLLEl-GS registers v2: `create_instance` + `create_device2`), driven
+    through our create-instance / create-device wrappers so the core injects its own
+    extensions/features and picks the queue;
+  - builds `retro_hw_render_interface_vulkan` (interface_version **5**) with `set_image`,
+    `get_sync_index{,_mask}`, `wait_sync_index`, `lock_queue`/`unlock_queue`, `set_command_buffers`
+    (logs-once stub — pgs never uses it), `set_signal_semaphore`;
+  - per frame: blit the core's `R8G8B8A8_UNORM` image into a `B8G8R8A8_UNORM` staging image (the
+    R↔B move that yields XRGB8888 byte order), `vkCmdCopyImageToBuffer` into a mapped host-visible
+    buffer, fenced, submitted under the shared queue lock; staging reallocates on extent change;
+    sync ring of 2.
+- **Go/config plumbing:** `Metadata.HwContext` ("", "gl", "vulkan"); `Video.vk` mutually exclusive
+  with `Video.gl`; env `GET_PREFERRED_HW_RENDER`→VULKAN, `SET_HW_RENDER` accepts Vulkan (no GL
+  fb/proc callbacks), env 43 (negotiation) + env 41 (`GET_HW_RENDER_INTERFACE`) wired;
+  `coreVideoRefresh` routes HW frames through `nano_vk_readback`. Lifecycle on the LibCo cothread:
+  `nano_vk_init` **before** `context_reset`; teardown `predestroy → context_destroy → shutdown`.
+  GL zero-copy is guarded off for Vulkan cores.
+
+All of it is gated behind `hwContext: vulkan` — inert for every existing core, so the single
+`worker.exe` stays safe on the mixed GL pool (verified: n64 GL room ran with GL zero-copy armed
+normally on the VK-capable binary).
+
+---
+
+## Acceptance criteria (spec §5)
+
+### 1. Stuntman/paraLLEl-GS reaches Playing, streams ≥30 s, screenshots show the game — **PASS**
+Multiple rooms reached `Playing` and streamed 40–55 s. `[game-override] option
+pcsx2_renderer=paraLLEl-GS` applied; frames flowed (client luma changed 0→9→65→88→108→119 across the
+boot/intro/menu).
+- **Colors correct (R/B order verified):** the Stuntman **main menu** rendered with a **gold** logo
+  underline and **red** background stars. A swapped R/B would have made the gold cyan and the stars
+  blue — they are correctly gold/red, confirming the `R8G8B8A8→B8G8R8A8` blit produces the right
+  XRGB8888 byte order.
+- The intro is b/w vintage FMV (spec-noted) and rendered correctly as grayscale.
+
+### 2. Log shows the negotiation + interface handshake, no "rejected non-GL" — **PASS**
+```
+[vk] negotiation interface stored (version 2, create_instance=yes create_device2=yes)
+[vk] instance created by core (v2 create_instance)
+[vk] physical device: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti (api 1.4.329)
+[vk] device created by core (v2 create_device2), queue family 0
+[vk] hw render interface ready (version 5)
+vulkan capture: device ready, hw render interface built (readback path)
+[vk] staging (re)allocated for 640x448
+```
+No `rejected non-GL hw render context` warning appeared. The interface_version is 5 (the core refuses
+anything else — main.cpp:1672).
+
+### 3. pace-diag ~60 ticks, perf-attr flows — **PASS**
+Under load (accelerator held), after boot/shader warm-up:
+```
+pace-diag: ticks/s=59.9 audio/s=47999 maxTick=8.2ms slowTicks(>20ms)=0 meanTick=3.72ms noSleep=0.0%
+[perf-attr] wall=5005ms ee_cpu=594ms gs_cpu=406ms gsidle=462ms mainloop=1193.0ms vswait=4437.2ms ...
+```
+`meanTick` ≈ 3.7 ms against a 16.6 ms budget — the synchronous readback (~1–2 ms) leaves ample
+headroom; a flat 60/48000 held. (`vidpush` reads 0 in perf-attr because that channel is the GL
+zero-copy metric; the readback cost lives inside mainloop.)
+
+### 4. Frame-size change survives; no "Internal data stream error"; video continues — **PASS (with caveat)**
+A `--resume` from a seeded save reached `Playing`, restored the VM ("deferred boot-restore done
+(warm-VM resume)"), and streamed 50 s. **No `Internal data stream error`** appeared in any Vulkan
+session (the ones present in `glworker-2.log` are all from earlier GL runs, pre-test). Video
+continued throughout.
+- **Caveat:** a live **448↔447** flip was **not captured** — Stuntman's intro/seeded-save content
+  stayed at 640×448 for the whole window, so the reallocation branch did not fire mid-run. The
+  realloc-on-extent-change code is implemented (`ensure_staging` + `vkDeviceWaitIdle`) and the
+  **initial** allocation is proven live; a live flip needs a test that drives into in-level gameplay
+  (the seeded save's autosave landed on the intro FMV). See Open questions.
+
+### 5. Room close clean 5× + mixed sequence — **SPLIT (see finding)**
+- **Without `skip_hw_context_destroy`** (the spec §2 arm): close **WEDGES**. `[vk] frontend resources
+  destroyed (pre context_destroy)` logs, then the core's `context_destroy` never returns; after 30 s
+  the room-close watchdog exits the worker (exit 70) and the runner respawns it. Reproduced on **both**
+  workers.
+  ```
+  [vk] frontend resources destroyed (pre context_destroy)
+  room ...Stuntman...: the core did not finish shutting down after 30s — it is wedged. Exiting ...
+  glworker EXITED exitcode=70 (0x00000046) - restarting in 4s
+  ```
+  Root cause is the **same** as the documented GL wedge (config comment lines 432–437): PCSX2's
+  `libretro_context_destroy` calls `MTGS::CloseGS()`, which deadlocks in our single-thread
+  (LibCo/`same_thread`) model. It is **renderer-independent** — GL hit it too — so this is not a
+  Vulkan-specific bug, and `context_destroy` is simply not survivable here.
+- **With `skip_hw_context_destroy`** (mirroring the shipped GL ps2 config): close is **CLEAN**.
+  ```
+  vulkan: skipping context_destroy (skip_hw_context_destroy hack set)
+  [vk] device + instance destroyed; loader unloaded
+  ```
+  4 clean closes, **no exit-70, no crash**. **Cross-room reuse works:** one worker process (never
+  restarted) hosted **three** Stuntman rooms back-to-back, each with a clean handshake and clean close
+  — my earlier worry that the core's static `vulkan_ctx` would fault on the next room did **not**
+  materialize (pgs `create_instance` resets it; our `nano_vk_shutdown` fully resets + reloads the
+  loader).
+- **Mixed sequence** (spec: vulkan → GL → vulkan on one process): confirmed on **one** worker process
+  (never restarted): GL n64 room (`GL zero-copy armed for n64`) → VK ps2 room (readback) → clean
+  close. GL cores stay inert to the VK changes and the two paths interleave cleanly.
+
+> Net: with `skip_hw_context_destroy` (the GL precedent), close + reuse are clean and repeatable. The
+> no-skip arm wedges, but the watchdog + respawn is the existing failsafe and the next room works.
+
+### 6. Git hygiene + `export-arcade-fork.ps1` — **PASS**
+Clean commits on `vulkan-capture-m1` (WIP carry-forward, vendored headers, implementation). The export
+script was run against this branch:
+```
+exporting 13852a7..vulkan-capture-m1 -> ...\fork.patch
+applies cleanly to 13852a7
+builds from the patch alone - the backup is real
+```
+i.e. the full branch (incl. the 1.3 MB vendored `vulkan_core.h`) applies to pristine upstream and
+compiles. Because M1 is pre-review and not merged, the repo's shipped `fork.patch` (which tracks
+`movietheater-fork` and must match the deployed worker) was **restored**; the compile-proven
+M1-inclusive patch is saved as `fork.vulkan-capture-m1.compile-proven.patch` (scratchpad). When M1
+merges to `movietheater-fork`, re-run `export-arcade-fork.ps1` (default branch) to regenerate the
+canonical `fork.patch`.
+
+---
+
+## Deviations from the spec
+
+- **Negotiation env number:** spec §2 calls it "env 47"; the actual constant in the vendored
+  `libretro.h` (and LRPS2's) is `RETRO_ENVIRONMENT_SET_HW_RENDER_CONTEXT_NEGOTIATION_INTERFACE =
+  43 | EXPERIMENTAL`. Implemented against the **symbolic** constant, so core/frontend agree regardless
+  of the numeric value.
+- **`skip_hw_context_destroy` for the test arm:** spec §2 said run *without* it and verify clean
+  close. I did — it **wedges** (reported above, criterion 5) — and then also tested *with* it to
+  establish the viable shippable config. Recommendation: ps2-Vulkan ships with `skip_hw_context_destroy`,
+  identical to the GL precedent.
+- **Physical-device selection:** I pass the explicit discrete GPU to `create_device2` (deterministic,
+  one GPU on the box) rather than `VK_NULL_HANDLE`. paraLLEl-GS accepts it; the header allows either.
+- **hw-render version log line** reads `Vulkan (version 4198400.0)` — that is
+  `VK_API_VERSION_1_1` packed into `version_major` by the core; cosmetic only.
+
+## Open questions for review
+
+1. **Ship ps2-Vulkan with `skip_hw_context_destroy`?** The MTGS::CloseGS deadlock is renderer-
+   independent and not fixable from the frontend. With the hack, close + cross-room reuse are clean.
+   This matches the GL row exactly. My `deinitVideoVulkan` already honors the hack (skips
+   `context_destroy`, still destroys device/instance) and reuse is proven clean. Recommend adopting it
+   for the shipped ps2-Vulkan profile. (The repo `config.worker-gl.yaml` ps2 entry was **not** changed;
+   only the deployed test configs were edited and then restored.)
+2. **Live 448↔447 flip:** needs a bench that reaches in-level gameplay (the seeded save's autosave sat
+   on the intro FMV, so it stayed 640×448). The realloc path is implemented and the initial alloc +
+   resume-without-pipeline-error are proven; a genuine mid-run flip is the one bit of criterion 4 not
+   yet observed live.
+3. **M2 hook:** the pool-image abstraction (`ensure_staging`) is kept separable from the readback so
+   the external-memory zero-copy (M2) can replace the staging copy without touching the interface/
+   negotiation code. No encoder/GStreamer code was touched.
+
+## Live-pool state at hand-off
+
+Fully restored to shipped state and verified: deployed `config.yaml` back to GL ps2 (OpenGL renderer,
+`skip_hw_context_destroy`, no `hwContext`); `game-overrides.json` regenerated from the DB via
+`arcade-gameconfig-export` (Stuntman → `Software (HW)`); the seeded user-33 save restored;
+`worker.exe` swapped back to the pre-test binary (my build kept as `bin/worker.vk.exe`); both workers
+recycled gracefully and a smoke room confirmed Stuntman runs on the shipped `Software (HW)` /
+OpenGL path again. No WEDGED flags, no leftover sentinels, all rooms free.
+
+---
+
+## Review response (2026-07-15, post-review revision)
+
+### F1 (blocking) — blit source extent under internal upscaling: addressed, with one factual correction
+
+**The correction first:** the prescribed mechanism (`image->create_info.extent`) does not exist.
+`retro_vulkan_image.create_info` is a **`VkImageViewCreateInfo`** (sType / image / viewType / format /
+components / subresourceRange) — it carries **no extent**, and Vulkan has no vkGetImageExtent. The
+spec §2's "create_info (contains the VkImage, format, extent)" carried the same assumption. A v5
+frontend **cannot** learn the image's extent from the interface; RetroArch (the normative reference)
+sizes the hw frame from `video_cb`'s width/height (gfx/drivers/vulkan.c `hw.last_width/last_height`),
+never from the image.
+
+**Why there is no crop bug:** the libretro contract is that `video_cb` w/h describe the frame, and
+paraLLEl-GS upholds it **including under high-res scanout**: `retro_get_system_av_info` doubles the
+base geometry when `pgs_high_res_scanout` is on (libretro/main.cpp:1533,1553-1558), and every
+`video_cb` receives `vsync.image->get_width()/get_height()` (GSRendererPGS.cpp:532,592). The image is
+never larger than what video_cb reports — so the readback naturally rides at the upscaled size; the
+"top-left crop" scenario cannot arise for this core.
+
+**Code change (the implementable form of the fix):** `cb_set_image` now stores the source format and
+explicit `src_w/src_h` fields; `nano_vk_readback` blits `srcOffsets[1]={src_w,src_h}` →
+`dstOffsets[1]={w,h}` with **VK_FILTER_LINEAR whenever they differ** and NEAREST for the 1:1 case
+(bit-preserving, the verified baseline). Today `src_w/src_h` resolve to the video_cb size (the only
+knowable extent); the structure is in place for an M3 core with a real extent side-channel.
+
+**Verification (as mandated) — paraLLEl-GS + `pcsx2_pgs_ssaa: "4x SSAA (ordered, can high-res)"` +
+`pcsx2_pgs_high_res_scanout: enabled`, live room 4H73HM:**
+```
+[game-override] option pcsx2_pgs_ssaa=4x SSAA (ordered, can high-res) for "Stuntman (USA)"
+[game-override] option pcsx2_pgs_high_res_scanout=enabled for "Stuntman (USA)"
+System A/V >>> 1280x896 (1280x1024), [59.94fps] ...      <- video_cb geometry IS the upscaled size
+[vk] staging (re)allocated for 1280x896                   <- staging picked up the larger extent
+pace-diag: ticks/s=59.9 audio/s=48003 maxTick=7.1ms slowTicks=0
+```
+Screenshot: the Stuntman main menu renders as the **full frame** (identical composition to the 1x run
+— logo, film-strip borders both edges), correct colors, at 1280×896 — **not a zoomed corner**. The
+encoder is fed 4× the pixels of the 1x arm.
+
+**Bonus: the live 448↔447 flip (criterion 4's missing piece) was captured in this run** — the menu
+cycle flips scanout height repeatedly and the extent-change reallocation fired live, with zero
+pipeline errors and the stream continuing:
+```
+[vk] staging (re)allocated for 1280x447
+[vk] staging (re)allocated for 1280x896
+[vk] staging (re)allocated for 1280x447
+[vk] staging (re)allocated for 1280x896   (repeating; no "Internal data stream error"; luma varying)
+```
+Criterion 4 is now fully observed live, at the high-res size no less.
+
+### N1–N3 — documented as code comments (no behavior change)
+- **N1**: `cb_wait_sync_index` carries a KNOWN LIMITATION comment (unsubmitted-fence race if a future
+  core calls it concurrently; paraLLEl-GS never calls it; revisit for M3 with a per-index submitted
+  flag).
+- **N2**: the `static VkPipelineStageFlags stages[8]` is annotated as safe only because the readback
+  is single-threaded on the cothread.
+- **N3**: the `nano_vk_shutdown` call site in `deinitVideoVulkan` documents that, with
+  `skip_hw_context_destroy`, the device dies with the core's PGS objects still referencing it —
+  accepted per the GL precedent, reuse verified clean across back-to-back rooms.
+
+### Hygiene
+Compile-proven patch regenerated for the revised branch (export script: applies cleanly to 13852a7 +
+builds); shipped `fork.patch` restored again (branch still pre-merge). Live pool restored: configs +
+DB-regenerated overrides (Stuntman → Software (HW)) + pre-test binary redeployed, workers recycled
+gracefully, all rooms free, no leftover backups/flags. Branch not pushed.
