+`coordinatorhandlers.go`: the room-layer `vkGame` block now calls the precedence (level 1 explicit field → level 2 renderer-option inference → level 3 core default), and stages `HwContextOverride` only when the resolved context **diverges** from the core default (same override-on-divergence contract `CoreLoad` already consumes; the escape-hatch `gl.enabled` term in `nanoarch.go:262` is untouched and still flips GL on for a resolved-"gl" room on a Vulkan-default core even with `isGlAllowed:false`).
