+## W8 — PSX to Beetle PSX HW (Vulkan): audit + recommendation (probe pending)
+
+Static audit of mednafen_psx_hw_libretro.dll (14.7 MB, nightly-synced): beetle_psx_hw_renderer value tokens
+**hardware_vk / hardware_gl / software**; vkCreateDevice + vkGetInstanceProcAddr present (Themaister's
+reference Vulkan negotiation — the one our frontend implements). beetle_psx_hw_internal_resolution tokens
+1x..16x; PGXP via beetle_psx_hw_pgxp_mode/_vertex/_texture; SAVE_RAM memcard via beetle_psx_hw_enable_memcard1.
+Vulkan likely routes around the config's noted GL-context blocker.
+
+**Save-continuity (the hard gate) — format is compatible.** Both pcsx_rearmed (pcsx_rearmed_memcard1: libretro)
+and beetle (beetle_psx_hw_enable_memcard1) expose PSX memcard 1 via RETRO_MEMORY_SAVE_RAM (.srm), and the real
+live saves (D:\ArcadeStorage\saves\*ps1*.srm, e.g. SotN, 007) are **131072 bytes = the standard 128 KB raw PSX
+memcard image** — a hardware standard both cores implement identically. So an existing pcsx .srm should be read
+byte-compatibly by beetle. Strong but not a live proof.
+
+**Recommendation:** beetle-Vk is technically viable and worth flipping for the PGXP/internal-res fidelity win —
+BUT do not flip live without two live proofs Eric gates: (1) a gated boot probe (CTR + SotN mode-switch
+1024x960<->640x480) confirming hardware_vk boots, zero-copy activates, and the caps-reneg survives SotN; (2) a
+save-continuity test — seed a COPY of a real .srm, boot on beetle-Vk, confirm the in-game load screen lists the
+existing save. Arm conservatively (PGXP off round 1; internal-res 2x, re-deriving scale from beetle's advertised
+base geometry, which differs from pcsx's software enhancement — read the System A/V line under hardware_vk). I
+did not flip ps1 (the save gate is unproven live and ps1 is healthy on GL).
